<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Heisler et al. (2010) pressurized SAM shell stress tensor, cortical microtubule alignment, PIN1-auxin phyllotactic mechanics, and (Pass 3) 3D multi-layered L1/L2/L3 Voronoi cell mesh with dynamic division planes — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring maps all 5 laws to papers and to line-pinned Lean 4 theorems (L35-L79), the math KG yaml registers equations -1..-5 with lean_code and code_locus, and function docstrings cite Louveaux 2016 / Besson-Dumais 2011 / Reddy 2004 for the division rules. However the hard-coded PIN1 noise constants (0.165, 0.155, 0.62-0.92 rad; L1163-L1166), the ablation asymptote 0.918 (L1271) and the compression factor 1.48 (L1281) have no source attribution, which is what made the v2 \"matches\" look emergent." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py L1163–L1166: Unattributed hard-coded PIN1 angular noise constants that determine the co-alignment statistic <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L1163-L1166>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Heisler et al. (2010) pressurized SAM shell stress tensor, cortical microtubule alignment, PIN1-auxin phyllotactic mechanics, and (Pass 3) 3D multi-layered L1/L2/L3 Voronoi cell mesh with dynamic division planes — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 adds a genuine 3D multi-layered mechanical model: four-sheet Voronoi polyhedral cells with exact volumes (`_voronoi_faces`, L356-L406; volume identity checked against ConvexHull in self-test 7), wall springs with a 5x stiffer L1 (`simulate_multilayer_sam_mesh`, L513-L937), turgor on exterior faces, elastic ghost supports, Jacobi-preconditioned relaxation (L615, L686), per-cell virial tension tensor (L692-L704), Lockhart creep with background growth (L687-L690), volume-doubling division with Louveaux-2016 / Besson-Dumais-2011 anticlinal planes and 3D Gibbs corpus planes (L418-L511), and the mesh -> L1-ODE coupling (L1041-L1066), backed by 5 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems. It is explicitly NOT a finite-element vertex model (L30-L33, L653: stress-free new contacts) and fails to reproduce the radial growth of the thin-shell anisotropy magnitude (bin-mean r = -0.11, apex artefact 0.059). The Pass 2 L1 ODE still hard-codes the PIN1 angular noise model that produces the co-alignment statistic (L1163-L1166) and the perturbation module uses a fitted asymptote and a 1.48 fudge factor (L1271-L1281), so the physics v2 credited at 94 is partly phenomenological." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py L1163–L1166: PIN1 polarity angle = CMT angle + N(0, 0.165) jitter, with 15.5 % 'switching cells' offset by U(0.62, 0.92) rad: the 84.9 % co-alignment is a hard-coded noise model, not an ODE outcome <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L1163-L1166>",
        "2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py L1271–L1281: Post-ablation circumferential fraction is an exponential relaxation to a hand-tuned asymptote 0.918; lateral-compression S_CMT uses comp_aniso * 1.48 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L1271-L1281>",
        "2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py L653–L653: New Voronoi contacts are inserted stress-free; no vertex degrees of freedom, wall bending or cell-volume constraint anywhere in the mesh (not a FEM / vertex model) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L653-L653>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-model-fidelity-6> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Heisler et al. (2010) pressurized SAM shell stress tensor, cortical microtubule alignment, PIN1-auxin phyllotactic mechanics, and (Pass 3) 3D multi-layered L1/L2/L3 Voronoi cell mesh with dynamic division planes — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1885-L2054) now reports 18 reference-anchored measurements, 9 of them new: flank L1 hoop-alignment fraction 0.8072 (PASS), L1 anisotropy vs membrane-law RMSE 0.0723 and dome-centre anisotropy 0.0589 (both FAILED, reported), L1 tension load share 0.7144 vs Law 4 0.7143 (PASS, model-internal reference), tension-rule shortest-plane fraction 0.3841 vs 0.71 (FAILED, binomial p = 5e-18), symmetric fraction 0.9756 vs 0.81 (FAILED), anticlinal new-wall fraction 1.0 (PASS, by construction), L3 periclinal 0.7059 vs uninformative 0.5 prior, mesh-vs-specimen profile RMS 5.54 um (FAILED). The 9 Pass 2 metrics are retained but three of them are now caveated as tuned/identity (co-alignment 0.8491 via the imposed jitter model, ablation fraction 0.9103 via the fitted asymptote, dome radius 50.0 um identity), which removes the basis for v2's 93." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
