<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) Pressurized Shell Principal Stress & 2:1 Cylinder Anisotropy Law" ;
    dct:description "Predicts isotropic tensile stress on the spherical SAM dome (driving hyper-dynamic isotropic microtubules), 2:1 circumferential hoop stress on cylindrical flanks, and amplified 5:1 crease stress at negative-Gaussian-curvature primordium boundaries | Variables: P: turgor pressure (MPa); R: shell curvature radius (um); t: L1 outer epidermal wall thickness (um); σ_θθ, σ_mm: circumferential and meridional principal tensile stresses (MPa); A_σ = (σ_1 - σ_2)/(σ_1 + σ_2): stress anisotropy" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322(5908):1650-1655 Figs. 1-2 & SOM Text S1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L148-L315>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L27-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sphere_hoop_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
def sphere_meridional_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
def cylinder_hoop_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := 2 * (P * R)
def cylinder_axial_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
theorem hamant_2008_pressurized_shell_anisotropy (P R : Int) :
    sphere_hoop_stress_2t P R - sphere_meridional_stress_2t P R = 0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R = 2 * cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R ∧
    3 * (cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R - cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R) =
      cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R + cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_θθ^dome = σ_mm^dome = PR/(2t) (A_σ = 0);  σ_θθ^cyl = PR/t = 2 σ_zz^cyl (A_σ = 1/3);  κ_m σ_m + κ_θ σ_θ = P/t" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.cylinder_hoop_stress_2t" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.hamant_2008_pressurized_shell_anisotropy" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kirsch / Hamant et al. (2008) Laser Ablation Wound Rim Hoop-Stress Doubling Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why single-cell or patch laser ablation in the L1 epidermis zeroes radial tension and doubles circumferential tension at the wound rim, reorienting both CMTs and PIN1 circumferentially around the ablation site | Variables: σ_∞: far-field isotropic dome membrane tension (MPa); a_0: laser ablation wound radius (um); r: radial distance from wound center (um)" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 3; Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8:e1000516 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L1231-L1315>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L61-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def kirsch_radial_scaled (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) : Int :=
  sig_inf * (r_sq - a0_sq)
def kirsch_hoop_scaled (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) : Int :=
  sig_inf * (r_sq + a0_sq)
theorem hamant_2008_ablation_rim_hoop_doubling (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) :
    kirsch_radial_scaled sig_inf a0_sq a0_sq = 0 ∧
    kirsch_hoop_scaled sig_inf a0_sq a0_sq = 2 * (sig_inf * a0_sq) ∧
    kirsch_radial_scaled sig_inf r_sq a0_sq + kirsch_hoop_scaled sig_inf r_sq a0_sq =
      2 * (sig_inf * r_sq)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_rr(r) = σ_∞(1 - a_0^2/r^2),  σ_θθ(r) = σ_∞(1 + a_0^2/r^2)  ⇒  σ_rr(a_0) = 0,  σ_θθ(a_0) = 2 σ_∞,  σ_rr + σ_θθ = 2 σ_∞" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.kirsch_hoop_scaled" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.hamant_2008_ablation_rim_hoop_doubling" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Heisler et al. (2010) & Jonsson et al. (2006) Stress- & Auxin-Coupled PIN1 Active Transport Conservation Law" ;
    dct:description "Couples PIN1 membrane allocation to both neighbor auxin concentration and cell-wall tensile stress orientation, generating golden-angle (137.5 deg) phyllotactic auxin maxima and synchronous PIN1/CMT reorientation | Variables: a_i: auxin concentration in L1 cell i; P_ij: PIN1 efflux carrier allocated to membrane i→j; e_1,i: maximal principal tensile stress eigenvector; T_PIN: active polar transport coefficient" ;
    dct:source "Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8(10):e1000516 Figs. 1-4; Jonsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103:1633-1638 Eqs. 1-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L960-L1228>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L91-L101> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_active_flux (T_pin P_ij P_ji a_i a_j : Int) : Int :=
  T_pin * (P_ji * a_j - P_ij * a_i)
theorem heisler_2010_pin1_flux_conservation (T_pin P_ij P_ji P_sym a_i a_j a : Int) :
    pin1_active_flux T_pin P_ij P_ji a_i a_j + pin1_active_flux T_pin P_ji P_ij a_j a_i = 0 ∧
    pin1_active_flux T_pin P_sym P_sym a a = 0
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_ij = P_tot exp(b_a a_j + b_σ |n_ij · e_1,i|^2) / Z_i;  J_{i←j} = T_PIN (P_ji a_j - P_ij a_i),  J_{i←j} + J_{j←i} = 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.pin1_active_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.heisler_2010_pin1_flux_conservation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) / Kutschera & Niklas (2007) Multi-layered L1/L2/L3 Pressurized Shell Load-Sharing Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Predicts that the stiff outer L1 wall carries the stiffness share k_1/Σk of the total turgor-driven shell tension (5/7 for the k_L1/k_inner = 5 assumption); checked numerically against the per-layer virial tension sums of the 3D Voronoi mesh (0.714 vs 0.714) and across the stiffness-ratio sweep | Variables: k_j: in-plane wall stiffness of layer j (L1 epidermis, L2 sub-epidermis, L3 corpus; k_1 = 5 k_inner); ε: common in-plane membrane strain; N_j: in-plane tension carried by layer j; P: turgor pressure; R: dome radius" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 SOM Text S1 (thick L1 outer wall); Kutschera & Niklas (2007) J. Plant Physiol. 164:1395-1409 (epidermal-growth-control theory)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L513-L957>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L107-L138> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def layer_membrane_tension (k eps : Int) : Int :=
  k * eps
theorem hamant_2008_multilayer_shell_load_sharing (k1 k2 k3 eps P R : Int)
    (h_laplace : 2 * ((k1 + k2 + k3) * eps) = P * R) :
    layer_membrane_tension k1 eps + layer_membrane_tension k2 eps + layer_membrane_tension k3 eps
      = (k1 + k2 + k3) * eps ∧
    layer_membrane_tension k1 eps * (k1 + k2 + k3) = k1 * ((k1 + k2 + k3) * eps) ∧
    2 * (layer_membrane_tension k1 eps + layer_membrane_tension k2 eps + layer_membrane_tension k3 eps)
      = P * R
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "N_j = k_j ε (compatible in-plane strain ε across glued layers);  Σ_j N_j = (k_1 + k_2 + k_3) ε;  N_1 / Σ N = k_1 / Σ k;  2 Σ N = P R (Laplace-Young recovered as the aggregate)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.layer_membrane_tension" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.hamant_2008_multilayer_shell_load_sharing" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Louveaux et al. (2016) Tension-Aligned Anticlinal Division Plane & Sachs Volume Bookkeeping Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Defines the mechanical (Louveaux 2016) division rule used for L1/L2 cells of the 3D mesh: the new anticlinal wall is placed along maximal tension; the Gibbs rule of Besson & Dumais (2011, β = 20.6) is the geometric alternative. Benchmarked against the 65-77 % shortest-plane and 81 % symmetric-division statistics of the shoot apex (the tension rule reaches only 0.38 shortest-plane, reported as a FAILED comparison) | Variables: n_s: outward surface normal of the L1/L2 cell; e_1: in-plane maximal-tension eigenvector of the cell tension tensor (tissue virial + cell-autonomous turgor term); n_div: normal of the new cell wall; V_1, V_2, V_mother: daughter and mother cell volumes" ;
    dct:source "Louveaux et al. (2016) PNAS 113(30):E4294-E4303; Besson & Dumais (2011) PNAS 108:6294-6299; Reddy et al. (2004) Development 131:4225-4237" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L418-L511>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L141-L172> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def cross_x (a2 a3 b2 b3 : Int) : Int := a2 * b3 - a3 * b2
def cross_y (a1 a3 b1 b3 : Int) : Int := a3 * b1 - a1 * b3
def cross_z (a1 a2 b1 b2 : Int) : Int := a1 * b2 - a2 * b1
def dot3 (x1 x2 x3 y1 y2 y3 : Int) : Int := x1 * y1 + x2 * y2 + x3 * y3
theorem louveaux_2016_anticlinal_tension_division_plane
    (n1 n2 n3 e1 e2 e3 V1 V2 Vm : Int)
    (h_sum : V1 + V2 = Vm) (h_sym : V1 = V2) :
    dot3 (cross_x n2 n3 e2 e3) (cross_y n1 n3 e1 e3) (cross_z n1 n2 e1 e2) n1 n2 n3 = 0 ∧
    dot3 (cross_x n2 n3 e2 e3) (cross_y n1 n3 e1 e3) (cross_z n1 n2 e1 e2) e1 e2 e3 = 0 ∧
    2 * V1 = Vm
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "n_div = n_s × e_1  ⇒  n_div · n_s = 0 (anticlinal: new wall contains the surface normal) and n_div · e_1 = 0 (new wall contains the maximal-tension direction);  V_1 + V_2 = V_mother, V_1 = V_2 ⇒ 2 V_1 = V_mother" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.dot3" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.louveaux_2016_anticlinal_tension_division_plane" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) Pressurized Shell Principal Stress & 2:1 Cylinder Anisotropy Law" ;
    dct:description "Predicts isotropic tensile stress on the spherical SAM dome (driving hyper-dynamic isotropic microtubules), 2:1 circumferential hoop stress on cylindrical flanks, and amplified 5:1 crease stress at negative-Gaussian-curvature primordium boundaries | Variables: P: turgor pressure (MPa); R: shell curvature radius (um); t: L1 outer epidermal wall thickness (um); σ_θθ, σ_mm: circumferential and meridional principal tensile stresses (MPa); A_σ = (σ_1 - σ_2)/(σ_1 + σ_2): stress anisotropy" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322(5908):1650-1655 Figs. 1-2 & SOM Text S1" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L148-L315>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L27-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def sphere_hoop_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
def sphere_meridional_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
def cylinder_hoop_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := 2 * (P * R)
def cylinder_axial_stress_2t (P R : Int) : Int := P * R
theorem hamant_2008_pressurized_shell_anisotropy (P R : Int) :
    sphere_hoop_stress_2t P R - sphere_meridional_stress_2t P R = 0 ∧
    cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R = 2 * cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R ∧
    3 * (cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R - cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R) =
      cylinder_hoop_stress_2t P R + cylinder_axial_stress_2t P R
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_θθ^dome = σ_mm^dome = PR/(2t) (A_σ = 0);  σ_θθ^cyl = PR/t = 2 σ_zz^cyl (A_σ = 1/3);  κ_m σ_m + κ_θ σ_θ = P/t" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.cylinder_hoop_stress_2t" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.hamant_2008_pressurized_shell_anisotropy" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Kirsch / Hamant et al. (2008) Laser Ablation Wound Rim Hoop-Stress Doubling Law" ;
    dct:description "Explains why single-cell or patch laser ablation in the L1 epidermis zeroes radial tension and doubles circumferential tension at the wound rim, reorienting both CMTs and PIN1 circumferentially around the ablation site | Variables: σ_∞: far-field isotropic dome membrane tension (MPa); a_0: laser ablation wound radius (um); r: radial distance from wound center (um)" ;
    dct:source "Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 Fig. 3; Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol. 8:e1000516 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py#L1231-L1315>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_033_auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics.lean#L61-L78> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def kirsch_radial_scaled (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) : Int :=
  sig_inf * (r_sq - a0_sq)
def kirsch_hoop_scaled (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) : Int :=
  sig_inf * (r_sq + a0_sq)
theorem hamant_2008_ablation_rim_hoop_doubling (sig_inf r_sq a0_sq : Int) :
    kirsch_radial_scaled sig_inf a0_sq a0_sq = 0 ∧
    kirsch_hoop_scaled sig_inf a0_sq a0_sq = 2 * (sig_inf * a0_sq) ∧
    kirsch_radial_scaled sig_inf r_sq a0_sq + kirsch_hoop_scaled sig_inf r_sq a0_sq =
      2 * (sig_inf * r_sq)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "σ_rr(r) = σ_∞(1 - a_0^2/r^2),  σ_θθ(r) = σ_∞(1 + a_0^2/r^2)  ⇒  σ_rr(a_0) = 0,  σ_θθ(a_0) = 2 σ_∞,  σ_rr + σ_θθ = 2 σ_∞" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jplph.2007.08.002>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1011866108>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1600677113>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1165594>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.01261>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.1000516>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pcbi.1002389> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Pressurized Thin-Shell Principal Stress Tensor, Nematic Microtubule Feedback & Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Transport" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.kirsch_hoop_scaled" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_033.hamant_2008_ablation_rim_hoop_doubling" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

